  "calibration_concern": "The analyst's moderate confidence is appropriate given the arithmetic errors in claims C2 and C4. The SELL recommendation is supported by the corrected fundamentals (operating income down ~41%, MCR up 3.6pp, medical costs up ~19%), but the report's credibility is undermined by calculation mistakes.",
  "overall_assessment": "Three of four claims contain arithmetic or presentation defects. Claim C3 is factually correct and well-supported. After correcting C1 (labeling), C2 (major arithmetic error: -51.26% vs -41.26%), and C4 (minor rounding: 18.86% vs 18.85%), the core investment thesis—deteriorating profitability driven by medical cost inflation—remains intact. The SELL recommendation is directionally sound but the report requires correction before dissemination."
